infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title When to event-source — and when not to
  desc Match the pattern to the entity's real requirements
  compares
    - label Strong fit
      children
        - label History is a compliance or legal requirement
          desc Financial, healthcare, regulated decisions — audit trail is a business need
        - label Temporal queries over past state in production
          desc Querying state as of a past date is a real need, not just debugging
        - label Domain must capture intent behind each change
          desc OrderApproved by reviewer vs AutoApproved by rule
        - label Team has real projection-pipeline experience
          desc Maintaining projections and lag is familiar, not new
    - label Poor fit
      children
        - label CRUD-heavy entity with no meaningful history
          desc Preferences, settings, session data, cache entries
        - label Only need fast querying of current state
          desc No audit requirement to justify the read-model cost
        - label Team new to projection infrastructure
          desc Lag management and upcasting are unlearned skills
        - label Tight delivery timeline
          desc Event sourcing raises initial delivery time significantly
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
